WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.310
Welcome to the Transhuman Daily, Friday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.550
Let's catch you up on the last 24 hours in transhumanism.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.300
Going the distance!

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:21.110
Brain implants in 14 paralysed people kept working for up to 7 years.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:26.760
And Neuralink got FDA approval for its pivotal trial, in people with ALS.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:38.390
DeepMind co-founder Shane Legg now rates minimal AGI before 2028 at about 65%.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:44.010
A Stanford physicist built a quantum gravity theory with help from OpenAI's AI.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.110
It's a preprint.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:47.600
And in another preprint,

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:52.300
OpenAI's AI helped design proteins; one in nine stuck in lab tests.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:54.200
In money experiments,

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:58.580
people who preferred human advisers still followed AI advice just as much.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.650
On to longevity. In eggs from older mice,

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:06.920
a designer protein glue kept chromosomes paired, like young eggs.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.170
In old mice, senolytics, drugs that clear out worn-out cells,

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:13.820
cut the liver tumours young mice never got.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:21.010
And judged by waist as well as weight, obesity went with 93% more dementia risk.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.610
Meanwhile, Denmark said no to Lilly's Alzheimer's drug Kisunla for routine use,

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:29.160
citing unclear benefit.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.310
Wellbeing now. In a small study,

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:36.120
a sleepless night left a telltale molecule in blood.

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:40.890
Across 43 studies, mindful people used social media more healthily.

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:44.960
And teen girls better at sensing their heartbeat liked their bodies more.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:45.960
Now, the catch.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:52.320
Swiss officials say hackers used AI agents in five recent attacks on companies and infrastructure.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.560
Closer to home,

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:59.020
76% of Australians say they've recently mistaken something AI-made for real.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:07.400
On the frontier, Arizona scientists made DNA cubes that build themselves into shapes,

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:08.770
like nano Minecraft.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:14.150
In a Utah trial, a man who lost a hand at 16 can feel his bionic grip.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:19.220
And Singapore made a whole district a robot test bed,

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:21.630
easing an ageing city's worker crunch.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:25.100
Implants that last, chromosomes that hold,

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:28.700
AI that helps with physics. Here's to going the distance!

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.550
Every day, the curve gets a little steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.950
Every day, the future shows up a little earlier.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.040
All of that, in one day. And the days keep getting bigger.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.340
That's the Transhuman Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.350
Go build the future. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.330
Want more? Meet us in North Sydney tonight.
